It is late Saturday afternoon.
I am standing in the kitchen in the flat.
The kitchen is full of steam and it smells wonderful.
Today I am taking my time.
I am cooking a real Mexican dinner.
Many fresh ingredients are lying on the table.
I chop tomatoes, onions, and garlic.
The vegetables are for the sauce.
Then I look at the mobile phone.
I have my mother's family recipe on there.
I want to be absolutely sure about the proportions.
How much chili do I need exactly?
I read through the recipe carefully one more time.
Then I add the spices to the large pot.
The sauce is simmering slowly on the stove.
I take a small spoon and taste it.
It is still missing a tiny bit of salt.
I stir the sauce and taste it again.
Now it is perfect and tastes exactly like home.
The food only needs twenty more minutes.
